# File spec for ./file_scan.rs — the offline twin of ./scan.rs. Delta versus the cluster
# scan lane is frozen only where visible from this file; the sibling is not specified here.

Spec: FileScan

Purpose:
  Provide the cluster-less `agent box file-scan` lane: parse a plain-YAML @FileScanSpec from
    disk, mount a @FileJukeBox over it and @cache_dir as the script-side `box`, expose an `args`
    map to the shipped `boxes/scan.rhai` script, and let that script persist the scanned package
    cache — build, script-dir and filter wiring only; the file itself contacts no API server and
    writes no status of its own beyond the cache directory.

References:
  ./mod.rs — the `boxes` dispatcher (spec pending): declares the private @file_scan module,
    awaits @file_scan::run, and owns the whole exit lane.
  /common/src/jukebox_file.sdd — @FileScanSpec is the spec-file shape and @FileJukeBox (via
    @FileJukeBox::new) is the box object; its spec owns every cache artifact the run leaves.
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script::new_file_scan engine assembly, the converted
    @Script::run_file channel, and the unconverted Deref'd core @ctx and @set_dynamic used here.
  /agent/scripts/boxes/scan.rhai — the script this run executes; its key probes explain the
    frozen `args` shape, its semantics are not this spec's.
  ./scan.rs — cluster-scan twin, read-comparison only; ./scan.sdd pending, no authority here.

Must:
  The execution order is frozen: build the engine first, read and parse the spec file second,
    create the cache directory third, then construct and bind the box/args, then run the script —
    so a missing spec or a malformed YAML exits before @cache_dir is ever created, and the engine
    construction performs no IO at all.
  The spec file is read with @tokio::fs::read_to_string and decoded with @serde_yaml::from_str
    straight into @FileScanSpec — there is no loader method, no existence pre-check, and no
    validation beyond serde: @FileScanSpec carries no required field, so even `{}` parses to both
    fields @None and the run continues.
  The engine is @Script::new_file_scan over exactly two resolver dirs, `<script_dir>/boxes` then
    `<script_dir>/lib` (joined by @Display, lossy), in that order; the file-scan surface it
    installs carries real http/s3 and the @FileJukeBox registrations only, so cluster-side script
    names fail as function-not-found on this lane.
  Two script globals are live before the run: `box` holds the owned @FileJukeBox
    (@FileJukeBox::new(spec, @cache_dir.clone()), infallible) pushed through the Deref'd
    @rhai::Scope @set_value, and `args` is pushed through the unconverted core @set_dynamic as an
    @serde_json::json! map freezing exactly the keys `file_scan` (always `true`), `cache_dir` and
    `script_dir` (both @to_string_lossy text), `filter`, and `namespace` (always `""`).
  An unset `filter` still ships the key: @Option serializes to JSON null, so `args.filter` is
    present-but-null, never a missing key — the scan script relies on this to distinguish the
    full-scan leg.
  The run target is the literal `<script_dir>/boxes/scan.rhai` @PathBuf; the script's last value
    is discarded (`let _ =`), only the @Err leg of @Script::run_file propagates.
  This file writes nothing to disk itself except the @tokio::fs::create_dir_all of @cache_dir
    (existing dirs are the silent no-op leg): `index.yaml`, per-package bundles and scan status
    exist only if the script calls the @FileJukeBox setters, and no statuses.json or CRD status
    is defined anywhere on this path.
  @run is @async and awaited by the dispatcher; both IO calls are @tokio::fs so a live tokio
    runtime is required, and no @kube::Client is ever constructed by this file.

Must not:
  Call @common::context::set_box or any other context/kube surface (unlike the cluster scan
    twin): the reconcile context stays @VynilContext::None, the script gets namespace `""` from
    `args`, and the only status sink is the cache directory.

Depends on:
  @common::rhaihandler::Script (/common/src/rhaihandler.sdd) — @Script::new_file_scan,
    @Script::run_file, and the public @ctx and @set_dynamic Deref targets.
  @common::jukebox_file::{@FileJukeBox, @FileScanSpec} (/common/src/jukebox_file.sdd) — input
    payload and mounted box.
  @common::{@Error, @Result} (/common/src/lib.rs) — @Error::Stdio and @Error::YamlError are the
    only variants this file produces; @Error::Core arrives from @Script::run_file.
  @tokio::fs, @serde_yaml, @serde_json — IO and the two decode/json! lanes.
  @clap::Args — the flag model of @Parameters.
  /agent/scripts/boxes/scan.rhai — external runtime payload, not compiled in; it must exist under
    @script_dir at run time.
  ./mod.rs — caller and exit-lane owner (spec pending), which invokes
    @common::context::init_k8s (a documented no-op) before dispatch.

Exposes:
  @Parameters — @clap::Args + @Debug + @Serialize + @Deserialize struct, pub only to the
    @boxes module (the @file_scan module itself is private to ./mod.rs), flagging exactly:
    `-S`/`--spec` → @PathBuf `spec`, required, no env, no default; `-c`/`--cache-dir` → @PathBuf
    `cache_dir`, required, no env, no default; `-s`/`--script-dir` → @PathBuf `script_dir`, env
    `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, default `./agent/scripts`; `-f`/`--filter` → @Option<@String> `filter`,
    env `SCAN_PACKAGE`, @None when unset. No `value_name` overrides on any flag.
  @file_scan::run — @pub @async fn taking a borrowed @Parameters and returning
    @common::Result<()>, awaiting one run of the whole flow above; the only success output is
    @Ok(()), never a value.

Accepts:
  A @Parameters reference by whatever route clap produced it (flags, env, and default legs); a
    readable, valid-UTF-8 YAML spec file; a @cache_dir path @create_dir_all can materialize; a
    @script_dir whose layout actually holds `boxes/scan.rhai` plus the `boxes`/`lib` module dirs.

Returns:
  @Ok(()) whenever the script completes — independent of how many packages the cache holds, which
    is entirely the script's outcome; the discarded @rhai::Dynamic last value carries nowhere.

Raises:
  @Error::Stdio (display `Stdio error {0}`) when the spec file is missing, unreadable or
    non-UTF-8, or when @create_dir_all fails on @cache_dir.
  @Error::YamlError (display `YamlError: {0}`, the @serde_yaml text verbatim) when the spec body
    is not valid YAML.
  @Error::Core from @Script::run_file: `Missing script <script_dir>/boxes/scan.rhai` when the
    script is absent, and `Rhai script error: ...` for every parse or run failure — including a
    scan the script itself rethrows after failing the box.
  The @Stdio and @YamlError texts here carry no stable unique identifier, unlike `SCAN-FILE-001`
    downstream (see Tasks).

Handles:
  Unset `--filter` / unset `SCAN_PACKAGE` — `args.filter` present as null, script takes its
    full-scan leg.
  Missing cache directory — created before the box is bound; a present one passes untouched.
  Env-fed defaults — `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY` steers the resolver dirs and the script path jointly,
    since all three paths derive from one @script_dir value; `SCAN_PACKAGE` supplies `filter`.
  Key-less or empty spec YAML — binds a box whose two spec fields are both @None and still runs the
    script; whether the run then succeeds or errors is decided inside the script, not here.
  Any @Err — the caller's lane: @boxes::run logs `File scan failed with: {e:}` via @tracing and
    calls @std::process::exit(1); @Ok(()) returns and the process exits 0; this file never exits
    itself.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover spec-file missing: @Err @Error::Stdio and @cache_dir still absent afterwards.
  [ ] Cover malformed YAML spec: @Err text starts `YamlError:`, @cache_dir still absent.
  [ ] Cover `{}` spec: @Ok path reaches the script with `box.spec` source/pull_secret unit — test
    needs a stub script_dir, proving no kube client is required end-to-end.
  [ ] Cover `args` shape against a stub script: five frozen keys, `file_scan` true,
    `namespace` `""`, and filter @None arriving as present-but-null.
  [ ] Cover absent `<script_dir>/boxes/scan.rhai`: @Err @Error::Core displaying
    `Missing script …`.
  [ ] Cover cache-dir creation: nested nonexistent @cache_dir exists after a successful stub run.
  [?] The @Serialize and @Deserialize derives on @Parameters are unused here — the args map is a
    hand-written @serde_json::json! with a different key set — decide whether the derives are
    dropped or @Parameters reuses them as the scan twin does with @serde_json::to_value.
  [?] `--spec` and `--cache-dir` refuse env/default while `--script-dir` and `--filter` accept
    env — decide whether the offline lane (made for Jobs-without-flags contexts) should be
    env-completable for all four flags.
  [?] The @Stdio and @YamlError texts from this file carry no stable unique id against the project
    error-tagging rule; decide whether file-scan errors get tagged like `SCAN-FILE-001`.
  [?] @init_k8s runs unconditionally in ./mod.rs before dispatch although this lane is built to
    need no cluster state; it is a no-op today, so decide whether the offline lane should be
    excluded when @init_k8s ever grows real behavior.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a mapped passing test or a recorded Task exemption, the coverage Tasks are
    green, and `cargo test -p agent` with `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` stay green.

Scenario: Missing spec file fails before touching the cache
  Given a @Parameters pointing @spec at a nonexistent path and @cache_dir at a fresh subdir
  When @run executes
  Then it returns @Err @Error::Stdio and the @cache_dir tree was never created
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Malformed spec YAML is a yaml error not a script error
  Given a spec file containing invalid YAML
  When @run executes
  Then it returns @Err whose display starts `YamlError: ` and the script is never started
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Empty spec still mounts an empty file box
  Given a spec file containing `{}`
  When @run executes
  Then the @FileJukeBox is bound with both fields @None and the run outcome is decided by the
    script alone
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Args map shape is frozen for the script
  Given any successful stub-script run with `--filter` unset
  When the script reads `args`
  Then `file_scan` is `true`, `namespace` is `""`, `cache_dir`/`script_dir` are the lossy path
    texts, and `filter` exists with a null value — never an absent key
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Missing scan script is a core missing-script error at exit 1
  Given a @script_dir without `boxes/scan.rhai`
  When the dispatcher awaits @run
  Then @Err @Error::Core displays `Missing script <script_dir>/boxes/scan.rhai`, the dispatcher
    logs it and exits 1; success would exit 0
  No mapped test exists.
